IMPORT prelude

-- Duties Act 2008 (Western Australia) -- the buyer of a home or of shares: what transfer duty, foreign transfer duty or
-- landholder duty must I pay, do I get a concession, and by when must I lodge, pay and apply.
--
-- SEAT: the buyer (of a home, or of shares in a company) -- the transferee or purchaser on whom Schedule 1 column 4 puts
-- the transfer duty, and the acquirer on whom Chapter 3 puts landholder duty. Every exported question is phrased as that
-- buyer would ask it. The car buyer's questions are in da-vehicles.l4.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 15 (dutiable property); Schedule 1 items s 11(1)(a), (b) and s 20 (who pays); s 23 (lodging, 2
-- months, fine $5 000); s 25 (when duty must be paid); s 26 and Schedule 2 Division 1 (the general rate); s 27 (dutiable
-- value: the greater of the consideration and the unencumbered value); Chapter 2 Part 6 Division 3, ss 141, 142A, 142(1),
-- 143(1), 144 (first home owner concessional rate and the time to apply), with Schedule 2 Division 2; Chapter 3, ss 155(2),
-- 161, 163, 184, 186, 188 (landholder duty on shares in a land-rich company); Chapter 3A Part 2, ss 205A, 205H, 205K, 205L,
-- 205M, 205O (foreign transfer duty, 7%); Chapter 6A, ss 266E-266I, 266K, 266L, 266O (the off-the-plan concession).
--
-- Edition: compilation of the Duties Act 2008 (Act No. 11 of 2008) as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49812.txt (legislation.wa.gov.au mrdoc 49812, retrieved 2026-09-07). The deposit states no
-- compilation number or date; its compilation table ends with the Help to Buy (Commonwealth Powers) Act 2025 Pt. 4 Div. 1 (in
-- operation 19 Dec 2025). The rates and thresholds are in the Act itself (Schedule 2, s 142(1)(b), s 266L); no regulation is
-- used. THE FORMULAS FOR X, Y, Z, A AND B IN s 266L(2), (3), (3A), (5) AND (6) are Word equations missing from the .txt
-- deposit; they are transcribed by hand from the authorised Word rendering of the same document (mrdoc 49812) in
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49812.formulas.md (2026-10-21), and encoded.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: every other dutiable transaction and the special dutiable value rules (ss 28-44A); exemptions, nominal duty and
-- the other concessions (Part 6 Divisions 1, 2 and 4); further concessional transactions (ss 142(2), 143(2)-(4)); the
-- clawback in s 145; the FHOG Act eligibility test itself (whether each transferee is a "concessional first home owner" is a
-- FACT: s 142A borrows it from the First Home Owner Grant Act 2000) and the FHOG Act meaning of "home" (a fact, s 141(2));
-- the metropolitan and Peel region boundaries (a fact, from the Planning and Development Act 2005); substituted transferees
-- (s 142(1)(a)(ii)); off-the-plan replacement agreements after a cancelled transaction (ss 266F(2), 266FA(2), 266H(2)) and
-- the multi-lot and aggregation rules (ss 266M, 266N); linked entities (ss 156-157), relevant arrangements (s 155(3)-(4)),
-- the s 189 reduction and the exemptions for landholder duty; foreign landholder duty (Chapter 3A Part 3) and foreign
-- corporations and trusts.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the seat of the buyer, with the design defaults ruled on
-- 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See
-- NOTES.md.

§ `Duties Act 2008 -- the buyer of a home or of shares`

§§ `Arithmetic used by the rates`

-- Schedule 2 charges "per $100 or part of $100": a part of $100 counts as a whole $100.
GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of 100-dollar parts in` MEANS
    IF FLOOR (`amount` DIVIDED BY 100) TIMES 100 EQUALS `amount`
    THEN `amount` DIVIDED BY 100
    ELSE FLOOR (`amount` DIVIDED BY 100) PLUS 1

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `s 26 and Schedule 2 Division 1 -- the general rate, as a table`

-- s 26(1): "Unless otherwise provided in this Chapter, duty is chargeable -- (a) by reference to the dutiable value of a
-- dutiable transaction; and (b) at the general rate of duty." (2): the rates "are set out in Schedule 2".
-- Schedule 2 Division 1, "Dutiable value (rounded down to nearest whole dollar)":
--   $0 - $120 000            $1.90 per $100 or part of $100
--   $120 001 - $150 000      $2 280 + $2.85 per $100 or part of $100 above $120 000
--   $150 001 - $360 000      $3 135 + $3.80 per $100 or part of $100 above $150 000
--   $360 001 - $725 000      $11 115 + $4.75 per $100 or part of $100 above $360 000
--   $725 001 and upwards     $28 453 + $5.15 per $100 or part of $100 above $725 000
-- A rate band: on whole dollars above `above`, the duty is `base amount` plus `per 100` for each $100 or part above it.

DECLARE `Rate band` HAS
    `above` IS A NUMBER
    `base amount` IS A NUMBER
    `per 100` IS A NUMBER

-- The table, highest band first (the first band whose floor the value exceeds is the one that applies).
`the general rate scale` MEANS
    LIST `Rate band` OF 725000, 28453, 5.15
         `Rate band` OF 360000, 11115, 4.75
         `Rate band` OF 150000, 3135, 3.80
         `Rate band` OF 120000, 2280, 2.85
         `Rate band` OF 0, 0, 1.90

GIVEN `scale` IS A LIST OF `Rate band`
      `whole dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the duty on the scale` MEANS
    CONSIDER `scale`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN `band` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN
        IF `whole dollars` GREATER THAN `band`'s `above`
        THEN `band`'s `base amount`
             PLUS `band`'s `per 100` TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`whole dollars` MINUS `band`'s `above`)
        ELSE `the duty on the scale` `rest` `whole dollars`

GIVEN `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the duty at the general rate` MEANS
    `the duty on the scale` `the general rate scale` (FLOOR `the dutiable value`)

@export What transfer duty would I pay at the general rate on this dutiable value (Schedule 2 Division 1)?
GIVEN `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER @desc The dutiable value of your purchase, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What duty would I pay at the general rate` IS
    `the duty at the general rate` `the dutiable value`

§§ `Chapter 2 Part 6 Division 3 and Schedule 2 Division 2 -- the first home owner concession, as a table`

-- s 142(1)(b): the unencumbered value "does not exceed -- (i) if the property is land that does not include a home --
-- $450 000; or (ii) if the property is land in the metropolitan region or the Peel region that includes a home -- $700 000;
-- or (iii) if the property is land outside the metropolitan region and the Peel region that includes a home -- $750 000."
-- Schedule 2 Division 2, s 143 First home owners ("rounded down to nearest whole dollar"):
--   does not include a home:                 $0 - $350 000 Nil;  $350 001 - $450 000 $15.39 per $100 or part above $350 000
--   metropolitan or Peel, includes a home:   $0 - $500 000 Nil;  $500 001 - $700 000 $13.63 per $100 or part above $500 000
--   outside both, includes a home:           $0 - $500 000 Nil;  $500 001 - $750 000 $11.89 per $100 or part above $500 000
-- s 141(2): a term with a meaning in the FHOG Act has that meaning here, so whether land "includes a home" is the FHOG Act's
-- question and a FACT. "metropolitan region" and "Peel region" come from the Planning and Development Act 2005 (s 141(1)):
-- which side a suburb is on is a FACT.

DECLARE `Kind of land` IS ONE OF
    `land that does not include a home`
    `land in the metropolitan or Peel region that includes a home`
    `land outside the metropolitan and Peel regions that includes a home`

DECLARE `First home owner row` HAS
    `cap` IS A NUMBER
    `scale` IS A LIST OF `Rate band`

GIVEN `the land` IS A `Kind of land`
GIVETH A `First home owner row`
`the first home owner table` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the land`
    WHEN `land that does not include a home` THEN
        `First home owner row` OF 450000, LIST `Rate band` OF 350000, 0, 15.39
                                               `Rate band` OF 0, 0, 0
    WHEN `land in the metropolitan or Peel region that includes a home` THEN
        `First home owner row` OF 700000, LIST `Rate band` OF 500000, 0, 13.63
                                               `Rate band` OF 0, 0, 0
    WHEN `land outside the metropolitan and Peel regions that includes a home` THEN
        `First home owner row` OF 750000, LIST `Rate band` OF 500000, 0, 11.89
                                               `Rate band` OF 0, 0, 0

§§ `The buyer and the purchase`

-- s 205A(1): "foreign individual means an individual who is not -- (a) an Australian citizen ...; or (b) the holder of a
-- permanent visa ...; or (c) the holder of a special category visa" (the Commonwealth Acts' terms, asked as FACTS).
DECLARE Buyer HAS
    `is an Australian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a permanent visa` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a special category visa` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Off-the-plan facts (Chapter 6A). `day entered into` is a date written as the number YYYYMMDD (2026-06-30 is 20260630).
DECLARE `Development stage` IS ONE OF
    `not an off-the-plan purchase`
    `before development for the subdivision commences`
    `after development commences but before it is completed`
    `after development is completed`

-- s 266E: an "eligible scheme" is a strata scheme or a community titles (building) scheme; a "single-tiered scheme" is one in
-- which no part of a floor of a lot "forms or joins the ceiling of another lot"; every other eligible scheme is multi-tiered.
DECLARE `Scheme tier` IS ONE OF
    `a multi-tiered scheme`
    `a single-tiered scheme`

-- One case is one purchase (one transfer or agreement for transfer), as the Act counts dutiable transactions.
DECLARE Purchase HAS
    `consideration` IS A NUMBER
    `unencumbered value` IS A NUMBER
    `land` IS A `Kind of land`
    `is residential property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `each transferee is a concessional first home owner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the buyers` IS A LIST OF Buyer
    `stage` IS A `Development stage`
    `scheme` IS A `Scheme tier`
    `day entered into` IS A NUMBER
    `lot will have a new dwelling` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner is of the opinion the dwelling is suitable as a residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an exclusion in s 266F(3) or s 266FA(3) applies` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `s 27 -- dutiable value`

-- s 27: the dutiable value is "(a) the consideration for the dutiable transaction; or (b) the unencumbered value of the
-- dutiable property ... if ... (iii) the unencumbered value is greater than the consideration for the transaction."
GIVEN `the purchase` IS A Purchase
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the dutiable value of` MEANS
    `the greater of` (`the purchase`'s `consideration`) (`the purchase`'s `unencumbered value`)

@export What is the dutiable value of my purchase (s 27)?
GIVEN `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc Your purchase
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my dutiable value` IS `the dutiable value of` `the purchase`

§§ `ss 142 and 143 -- first home owner concessional transaction and rate`

-- s 142(1): "(a) ... each transferee is a concessional first home owner; and (b) the unencumbered value of the dutiable
-- property ... does not exceed" the cap for its kind of land.
-- s 143(1): "Duty is chargeable on a first home owner concessional transaction at the applicable concessional rate of duty."
GIVEN `the purchase` IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a first home owner concessional transaction` IF
        `the purchase`'s `each transferee is a concessional first home owner`
    AND `the purchase`'s `unencumbered value` AT MOST (`the first home owner table` (`the purchase`'s `land`))'s `cap`

@export Is my purchase a first home owner concessional transaction (s 142(1))?
GIVEN `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc Your purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my purchase a first home owner concessional transaction` IF
    `it is a first home owner concessional transaction` `the purchase`

-- Transfer duty before any off-the-plan reduction: the concessional rate where s 142(1) is met, otherwise the general rate.
GIVEN `the purchase` IS A Purchase
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the transfer duty before the off-the-plan concession` MEANS
    IF `it is a first home owner concessional transaction` `the purchase`
    THEN `the duty on the scale` ((`the first home owner table` (`the purchase`'s `land`))'s `scale`)
                                 (FLOOR (`the dutiable value of` `the purchase`))
    ELSE `the duty at the general rate` (`the dutiable value of` `the purchase`)

§§ `Chapter 3A Part 2 -- foreign transfer duty`

-- s 205H(1)(a), (b): a transfer, or an agreement for the transfer, "of residential property to a foreign person" is a foreign
-- dutiable transaction. s 205K(1): liable if "(a) liable to pay transfer duty on the transaction; and (b) a foreign person."
-- s 205L: "joint tenants of residential property are taken to hold the property as tenants in common in equal shares."
-- s 205O: "Foreign transfer duty is chargeable at the rate of 7% of the dutiable value of the foreign dutiable transaction."
-- INFERENCE (not in these words): with several buyers holding equal shares, the 7% falls on the share of each foreign buyer.
GIVEN `the buyer` IS A Buyer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the buyer is a foreign individual` IF
        (NOT (`the buyer`'s `is an Australian citizen`))
    AND (NOT (`the buyer`'s `holds a permanent visa`))
    AND (NOT (`the buyer`'s `holds a special category visa`))

@export Am I a foreign individual for foreign transfer duty (s 205A)?
GIVEN `the buyer` IS A Buyer @desc You
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a foreign individual` IF `the buyer is a foreign individual` `the buyer`

GIVEN `buyers` IS A LIST OF Buyer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of buyers in` MEANS
    CONSIDER `buyers`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN `b` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN 1 PLUS `the number of buyers in` `rest`

GIVEN `buyers` IS A LIST OF Buyer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of foreign buyers in` MEANS
    CONSIDER `buyers`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN `b` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN
        (IF `the buyer is a foreign individual` `b` THEN 1 ELSE 0) PLUS `the number of foreign buyers in` `rest`

GIVEN `the purchase` IS A Purchase
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the foreign transfer duty before the off-the-plan concession` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the purchase`'s `is residential property`)) OR (`the number of buyers in` (`the purchase`'s `the buyers`) EQUALS 0)
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the dutiable value of` `the purchase` TIMES 7 DIVIDED BY 100
         TIMES `the number of foreign buyers in` (`the purchase`'s `the buyers`)
         DIVIDED BY `the number of buyers in` (`the purchase`'s `the buyers`)

§§ `Chapter 6A -- the off-the-plan concession`

-- s 266F(1): a concessional preconstruction agreement is "(a) an agreement for the purchase, from the owner of land to be
-- subdivided by the registration of an eligible scheme ..., of a lot in the scheme on which there will be a new dwelling; and
-- (b) entered into before development for the subdivision commences; and (c) entered into in the period -- (i) if the
-- eligible scheme is a multi-tiered scheme -- beginning on 23 October 2019 and ending on 30 June 2026; or (ii) if the eligible
-- scheme is a single-tiered scheme -- beginning on 21 March 2025 and ending on 30 June 2026."
-- s 266FA(1): a concessional under construction agreement is the same but "(b) entered into after development for the
-- subdivision commences, but before development for the subdivision is completed; and (c) ... (i) multi-tiered ... beginning
-- on 31 August 2023 and ending on 30 June 2026; or (ii) single-tiered ... beginning on 21 March 2025 and ending on 30 June 2026."
-- s 266G(1): a new dwelling may lawfully be used as a residence, "(b) in the Commissioner's opinion, is suitable to be used as
-- a place of residence", is intended to be so used, and is not an existing building. The Commissioner's opinion is asked
-- conditionally, as a fact. ss 266F(3) and 266FA(3) (rebate paid, replacement and subsale transactions and the like) are one
-- fact here.

GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER, `first` IS A NUMBER, `last` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day falls between` IF `the day` AT LEAST `first` AND `the day` AT MOST `last`

GIVEN `the purchase` IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lot qualifies` IF
        `the purchase`'s `lot will have a new dwelling`
    AND `the purchase`'s `the Commissioner is of the opinion the dwelling is suitable as a residence`
    AND (NOT (`the purchase`'s `an exclusion in s 266F(3) or s 266FA(3) applies`))

GIVEN `the purchase` IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a concessional preconstruction agreement` IF
        `the lot qualifies` `the purchase`
    AND `the day falls between` (`the purchase`'s `day entered into`) (`preconstruction window opens` `the purchase`) 20260630
    AND CONSIDER `the purchase`'s `stage`
        WHEN `before development for the subdivision commences` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE
        `preconstruction window opens` `p` MEANS
            CONSIDER `p`'s `scheme`
            WHEN `a multi-tiered scheme` THEN 20191023
            WHEN `a single-tiered scheme` THEN 20250321

GIVEN `the purchase` IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a concessional under construction agreement` IF
        `the lot qualifies` `the purchase`
    AND `the day falls between` (`the purchase`'s `day entered into`) (`under construction window opens` `the purchase`) 20260630
    AND CONSIDER `the purchase`'s `stage`
        WHEN `after development commences but before it is completed` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE
        `under construction window opens` `p` MEANS
            CONSIDER `p`'s `scheme`
            WHEN `a multi-tiered scheme` THEN 20230831
            WHEN `a single-tiered scheme` THEN 20250321

@export Is my agreement a concessional off-the-plan agreement (Chapter 6A, ss 266F and 266FA)?
GIVEN `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc Your purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my agreement a concessional off-the-plan agreement` IF
        `it is a concessional preconstruction agreement` `the purchase`
    OR  `it is a concessional under construction agreement` `the purchase`

-- s 266L(1) Table (preconstruction) and s 266L(4) Table (under construction): the concession percentage by concession day
-- and dutiable value. A row: on concession days from `first day` to `last day`, a dutiable value at or under `low band at
-- most` takes `low percentage`, one at or over `high band at least` takes `high percentage`, and one in between takes the
-- percentage from the formula in s 266L(2), (3), (3A), (5) or (6) (transcribed in mrdoc_49812.formulas.md):
--   (2) item 4   X = 100 - ((V - 500 000) / 100 x 0.05)      (3)  item 7   Y = 100 - ((V - 650 000) / 100 x 0.05)
--   (3A) item 10 Z = 100 - ((V - 750 000) / 100 x 0.05)      (5)  item 2   A = 75 - ((V - 650 000) / 100 x 0.0375)
--   (6) item 5   B = 75 - ((V - 750 000) / 100 x 0.0375)
-- Each starts at the row's `low percentage` at its `low band at most` and falls by `step per $100` for every $100 of V above
-- it, so the row carries that step. Items 1 and 2 of the s 266L(1) Table have no middle band (step 0).
-- s 266H(1)(a): the concession day is "the day on which the agreement is entered into" (the s 266H(2) replacement case is
-- not encoded).
DECLARE `Concession row` HAS
    `first day` IS A NUMBER
    `last day` IS A NUMBER
    `low band at most` IS A NUMBER
    `high band at least` IS A NUMBER
    `low percentage` IS A NUMBER
    `high percentage` IS A NUMBER
    `step per $100` IS A NUMBER

-- s 266L(1) Table, items 1-11. Items 1 and 2 apply to "Any dutiable value" (one band, a cap no value reaches).
`the preconstruction table` MEANS
    LIST `Concession row` OF 20191023, 20211023, 999999999999, 999999999999, 75,  75, 0
         `Concession row` OF 20211024, 20220531, 999999999999, 999999999999, 50,  50, 0
         `Concession row` OF 20220601, 20230510, 500000,       600000,       100, 50, 0.05
         `Concession row` OF 20230511, 20250320, 650000,       750000,       100, 50, 0.05
         `Concession row` OF 20250321, 20260630, 750000,       850000,       100, 50, 0.05

-- s 266L(4) Table, items 1-6.
`the under construction table` MEANS
    LIST `Concession row` OF 20230831, 20250320, 650000, 750000, 75, 37.5, 0.0375
         `Concession row` OF 20250321, 20260630, 750000, 850000, 75, 37.5, 0.0375

GIVEN `table` IS A LIST OF `Concession row`
      `the day` IS A NUMBER
      `the value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the concession percentage from` MEANS
    CONSIDER `table`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN `row` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN
        IF `the day falls between` `the day` (`row`'s `first day`) (`row`'s `last day`)
        THEN IF `the value` AT MOST `row`'s `low band at most`
             THEN `row`'s `low percentage`
             ELSE IF `the value` AT LEAST `row`'s `high band at least`
                  THEN `row`'s `high percentage`
                  ELSE `row`'s `low percentage` MINUS
                         ((`the value` MINUS `row`'s `low band at most`) DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES `row`'s `step per $100`)
        ELSE `the concession percentage from` `rest` `the day` `the value`

GIVEN `the purchase` IS A Purchase
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the concession percentage` MEANS
    IF `it is a concessional preconstruction agreement` `the purchase`
    THEN `the concession percentage from` `the preconstruction table` (`the purchase`'s `day entered into`)
             (`the dutiable value of` `the purchase`)
    ELSE IF `it is a concessional under construction agreement` `the purchase`
         THEN `the concession percentage from` `the under construction table` (`the purchase`'s `day entered into`)
                  (`the dutiable value of` `the purchase`)
         ELSE 0

-- s 266I: the unadjusted duty amount is the transfer duty (and any foreign transfer duty) "that would be payable on the
-- agreement if it were not a concessional off-the-plan agreement".
-- s 266L(1), (4): the concession amount is "the lesser of -- (a) $50 000; (b) ... that percentage by the unadjusted duty
-- amount".
GIVEN `the purchase` IS A Purchase
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the unadjusted duty amount` MEANS
    `the transfer duty before the off-the-plan concession` `the purchase`
    PLUS `the foreign transfer duty before the off-the-plan concession` `the purchase`

GIVEN `the purchase` IS A Purchase
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the concession amount` MEANS
    `the lesser of` 50000 (`the concession percentage` `the purchase` TIMES `the unadjusted duty amount` `the purchase` DIVIDED BY 100)

@export How much off-the-plan concession do I get (s 266L)?
GIVEN `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc Your purchase
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much off-the-plan concession do I get` IS `the concession amount` `the purchase`

§§ `What I pay -- s 266K applied to transfer duty and foreign transfer duty`

-- s 266K(2), (3): the transfer duty is reduced first, "by so much of the concession amount as is necessary to reduce the
-- amount of transfer duty payable to zero"; any remainder reduces the foreign transfer duty.
GIVEN `the purchase` IS A Purchase
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the concession applied to transfer duty` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`the concession amount` `the purchase`) (`the transfer duty before the off-the-plan concession` `the purchase`)

@export What transfer duty must I pay on my purchase?
GIVEN `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc Your purchase
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What transfer duty must I pay` IS
    `the transfer duty before the off-the-plan concession` `the purchase`
    MINUS `the concession applied to transfer duty` `the purchase`

@export What foreign transfer duty must I (and my co-buyers) pay on my purchase (Chapter 3A)?
GIVEN `the purchase` IS A Purchase @desc Your purchase
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What foreign transfer duty must I pay` IS
    `the foreign transfer duty before the off-the-plan concession` `the purchase`
    MINUS (`the concession amount` `the purchase` MINUS `the concession applied to transfer duty` `the purchase`)

§§ `Schedule 1, s 20, ss 23, 25, 144, 205M and 266O -- who pays, and by when`

-- Schedule 1, s 11(1)(a) transfer: liability arises "When the property is transferred", payable by the "Transferee";
-- s 11(1)(b) agreement for transfer: "When the agreement is made", payable by the "Purchaser or transferee" (s 19, s 20).
@export As the buyer, am I the person liable to pay the transfer duty (s 20 and Schedule 1)?
GIVEN `I am the transferee or purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the property is transferred, or agreed to be transferred, to you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I pay the transfer duty` IF `I am the transferee or purchaser`

-- s 23(1): the person liable "must lodge" the instrument or a transfer duty statement "within 2 months after the day on which
-- liability for duty on the transaction arises. Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
@export Within how many months after liability arises must I lodge the transfer document or statement (s 23)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many months must I lodge` IS 2

@export What is the most I can be fined for not lodging in time (s 23 and s 205M)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for not lodging` IS 5000

-- s 205M(1): the person liable to foreign transfer duty "must lodge a foreign transfer duty declaration in the approved form
-- within 2 months after the day on which liability ... arises. Penalty ...: a fine of $5 000."
@export Within how many months must I lodge a foreign transfer duty declaration (s 205M)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many months must I lodge a foreign transfer duty declaration` IS 2

-- s 25(1): pay "within one month after the date of the assessment notice", unless (2) "within 12 months after the day on
-- which liability ... arises if the transaction is -- (a) a conditional agreement; or (b) ... if a document relating to the
-- transaction must be registered under ... the Transfer of Land Act 1893", or (3) "within 3 years ... if the transaction is
-- (a) a subdivision conditional agreement; or (b) an issue of title conditional agreement." s 205N says the same for foreign
-- transfer duty.
DECLARE `Time to pay` IS ONE OF
    `within one month after the assessment notice`
    `within 12 months after liability arises`
    `within 3 years after liability arises`

@export By when must I pay the duty (s 25)?
GIVEN `it is a conditional agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your contract is a conditional agreement
      `it must be registered under the Transfer of Land Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a document for your purchase must be registered under the Transfer of Land Act 1893
      `it is a subdivision or issue of title conditional agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your contract is conditional on a subdivision or on the issue of a title
GIVETH A `Time to pay`
DECIDE `By when must I pay the duty` IS
    IF `it is a subdivision or issue of title conditional agreement`
    THEN `within 3 years after liability arises`
    ELSE IF `it is a conditional agreement` OR `it must be registered under the Transfer of Land Act`
         THEN `within 12 months after liability arises`
         ELSE `within one month after the assessment notice`

-- s 144(2)(a)(i): a reassessment for a first home owner concessional transaction may be sought only up to "whichever is the
-- later of the day that is -- (I) 12 months after the day on which the first home owner concessional transaction was
-- completed; or (II) if an application for a first home owner grant has been made, 3 months after the day on which the grant
-- is paid". Counted here in whole months from completion.
@export Up to how many months after completion may I apply for the first home owner rate by reassessment (s 144(2))?
GIVEN `I applied for the grant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied for a first home owner grant
      `months from completion to the grant being paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months after completion the grant was paid
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Up to how many months after completion may I seek the first home owner rate` IS
    IF `I applied for the grant`
    THEN `the greater of` 12 (`months from completion to the grant being paid` PLUS 3)
    ELSE 12

-- s 266O(1): the application for the off-the-plan concession "must be made in the approved form no later than 12 months
-- after the day on which the agreement is completed" (completed: when the buyer becomes owner of the lot, s 266O(3)).
@export Within how many months of completion must I apply for the off-the-plan concession (s 266O)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many months must I apply for the off-the-plan concession` IS 12

§§ `s 15 -- are shares dutiable property`

-- s 15: "Any of the following is dutiable property -- (a) land in Western Australia; (b) a right; (c) a chattel in Western
-- Australia; (d) a Western Australian business asset." Shares are not in the list; s 79's "business asset" does not name
-- them. (That a share is not a "chattel" is an INFERENCE from the ordinary meaning.)
DECLARE `Kind of property` IS ONE OF
    `land in Western Australia`
    `land outside Western Australia`
    `a right`
    `a chattel in Western Australia`
    `a Western Australian business asset`
    `shares in a company`

@export Is what I am buying dutiable property for transfer duty (s 15)?
GIVEN `the property` IS A `Kind of property` @desc What you are buying
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I am buying dutiable property` IF
    CONSIDER `the property`
    WHEN `land outside Western Australia` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `shares in a company` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Chapter 3 -- landholder duty on shares in a land-rich company`

-- s 155(2): "An entity is a landholder if immediately before the acquisition -- (a) it is entitled to land assets in Western
-- Australia or an entity linked to the entity is so entitled; and (b) the total value of all such entitlements is
-- $2 000 000 or more." (Linked entities' holdings are included in the input figure.)
-- s 161: "significant interest ... (a) if the landholder is a listed landholder -- an interest of at least 90%; or
-- (b) otherwise -- an interest of at least 50%."
-- s 163(1): a relevant acquisition is crossing into a significant interest, or increasing one already held.
-- s 184(1): duty "at the general rate of duty set out in Schedule 2"; s 188(1), (3): on "the same percentage of the value of
-- the landholder as the percentage of the interest"; s 186(1): the value of the landholder is the unencumbered value of its
-- WA land assets and chattels. The s 189 reduction is not encoded.
DECLARE Company HAS
    `is listed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `value of land assets in Western Australia` IS A NUMBER
    `value of land assets and chattels in Western Australia` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the company` IS A Company
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company is a landholder` IF
    `the company`'s `value of land assets in Western Australia` AT LEAST 2000000

GIVEN `the company` IS A Company
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the significant interest` MEANS
    IF `the company`'s `is listed` THEN 90 ELSE 50

GIVEN `the company` IS A Company, `interest before` IS A NUMBER, `interest after` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a relevant acquisition` IF
        `the company is a landholder` `the company`
    AND (    (`interest before` LESS THAN `the significant interest` `the company`
              AND `interest after` AT LEAST `the significant interest` `the company`)
         OR  (`interest before` AT LEAST `the significant interest` `the company`
              AND `interest after` GREATER THAN `interest before`))

@export Must I pay landholder duty on the shares I am acquiring (Chapter 3)?
GIVEN `the company` IS A Company @desc The company whose shares you are acquiring
      `interest before` IS A NUMBER @desc Your interest (with associates) before the acquisition, as a percentage
      `interest after` IS A NUMBER @desc Your interest (with associates) after the acquisition, as a percentage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I pay landholder duty` IF
    `it is a relevant acquisition` `the company` `interest before` `interest after`

@export What landholder duty must I pay on the shares I am acquiring (ss 184, 186, 188)?
GIVEN `the company` IS A Company @desc The company whose shares you are acquiring
      `interest before` IS A NUMBER @desc Your interest (with associates) before the acquisition, as a percentage
      `interest after` IS A NUMBER @desc Your interest (with associates) after the acquisition, as a percentage
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What landholder duty must I pay` IS
    IF `it is a relevant acquisition` `the company` `interest before` `interest after`
    THEN `the duty at the general rate`
             (`the company`'s `value of land assets and chattels in Western Australia` TIMES `interest after` DIVIDED BY 100)
    ELSE 0
